WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.590
Rotten Tomatoes aggregates movie reviews and
uses them to give every movie a percentage

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.660
rating indicating their agreed-upon quality.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.540
But just because something has a low rating
on Rotten Tomatoes doesn't mean you shouldn't

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:12.040
watch it.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.500
This is especially true for genres like science
fiction, which tend to get reviewed especially

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.000
harshly.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.580
So we've put together a list of sci-fi movies
that are rated quite low on Rotten Tomatoes,

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:22.740
but are still worth watching.

00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:26.480
Some of them are good but misunderstood, and
some of them are bad but interesting.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:30.000
Either way, don't let the critics dissuade
you from giving these movies a look.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:31.520
Speed Racer

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:36.720
You've probably heard plenty of defenses of
the Wachowski siblings' Speed Racer by now.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:41.120
A bomb upon its 2008 release, it's since become
a beloved cult classic.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:46.540
Based on the American localization of a Japanese
anime, the movie rejected realism in favor

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:51.820
of oversaturated futuristic visuals and characters
with looks and names right out of the cartoon.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.480
But to the surprise of many, there's no parody
or cynicism in Speed Racer.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:09.140
The characters are played as real people with
emotions and believable motivations, and Speed

00:01:09.159 --> 00:01:14.500
Racer in particular is a very sincere young
man who just wants to be the best at the only

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:15.220
thing he's good at.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.760
The racing scenes are a delightful mix of
speed, color, and editing.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:23.420
Speed Racer isn't just a weird movie worth
watching, it's a genuinely great film that

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.840
the public just failed to appreciate upon
its release.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:27.740
Last Action Hero

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:34.000
Arnold Schwarzenegger was a megastar in 1993,
and Last Action Hero was intended to be a

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.420
huge summer blockbuster, but it became a legendary
flop.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.180
Critics hated it, and audiences just didn't
have time for it.

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:44.320
What's interesting about Last Action Hero
is also what ultimately makes it a failure:

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:49.820
it's a parody of over-the-top action films
that allows itself to become an over-the-top

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:50.520
action film.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:55.500
It satirizes overused tropes and then turns
around and uses them with barely a wink.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:02:00.439
Schwarzenegger plays Jack Slater, the hero
of a series of action films who finds his

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:05.180
way into the real world, but he also turns
up as himself in the "real world" scenes.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.340
"Wait, where are you going?"

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.280
"I'll be back.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:10.340
HAH!

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:12.000
Didn't know I was gonna say that, didn't you?"

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.180
"That's what you always say!"

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:20.350
It doesn't all quite hold together, but it's
still entertaining, and some excellent performances

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:24.580
along with the grand scale of what it's trying
to do narratively make it an interesting watch.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:26.440
Jupiter Ascending

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:30.891
Jupiter Ascending is the second Wachowski
film on this list, and it won't be at all

00:02:30.891 --> 00:02:35.200
surprising if it becomes as much of a cult
classic as Speed Racer, once a little more

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:36.000
time has passed.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.780
The major flaw of Jupiter Ascending is that
it tries to do too much.

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:44.840
Mila Kunis stars as Jupiter Jones, a poor
girl from Earth who finds out she's next in

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:47.300
line for a vast inheritance from outer space.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:51.800
Channing Tatum plays a wolf man from space
who's assigned to protect her from the many

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:53.370
forces aligned against her.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:58.700
Chief among those forces is Eddie Redmayne,
who plays an evil alien who's human in appearance

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.760
but unmistakably reptilian in demeanor.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:06.500
There are certainly valid criticisms about
the movie: the plot is definitely convoluted,

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.380
and some of the dialogue isn't great.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:12.150
But a lot of the critics that contributed
to Jupiter Ascending's low Rotten Tomatoes

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:16.460
score seem to have a problem with the basics
of the space opera subgenre.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:20.200
It may not be a perfect movie, but time will
almost certainly be kind to it.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:21.960
Event Horizon

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:27.010
Despite its bad reviews, Event Horizon might
be the most frightening outer space horror

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.920
film that doesn't involve facehuggers or xenomorphs.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:35.260
In fact, there are no aliens in this movie
at all, unless you count an unseen and shapeless

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:35.760
evil.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:40.540
The Event Horizon was a ship equipped with
a new kind of inter-dimensional warp drive,

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:43.140
which disappeared on its test flight seven
years earlier.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:46.870
Now it has reappeared near Neptune, and another
ship is sent to investigate.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:52.220
What the crew finds is a ghost ship that seems
to have recently returned from Hell itself.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:56.520
One by one, they encounter manifestations
of their dreams and nightmares, and most of

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:57.400
them don't survive.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:01.320
This is a grisly and disturbing movie that's
definitely not for everyone.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:05.400
But if you like horror, the "haunted house
in space" premise is interesting, and the

00:04:05.401 --> 00:04:06.780
scares are definitely there.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.280
"What do you think you're doing, Doc?"

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:15.920
"You wanted to know where the ship has been…
so now you'll find out!"

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.900
Masters of the Universe

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.100
Masters of the Universe is a big, glorious
mess.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:26.840
Adapted from the popular line of toys, it
probably earned its low Rotten Tomatoes rating,

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:31.190
but it's still pretty fun, especially if you're
into that Cannon Films VHS aesthetic.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:35.780
Dolph Lundgren plays He-Man, the barbarian
hero who must defeat Skeletor, played here

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:36.940
by Frank Langella.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.960
"You dare threaten her life?"

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.860
"I dare anything!

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.140
I am Skeletor."

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:48.940
The film contains very little of the mythology
from the Masters of the Universe cartoon and

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:54.680
comics, but it tells a pretty fun action-oriented
story about an eternal war in a sci-fi/fantasy

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.460
world spilling into 1980s Earth.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:05:01.000
Most of the cast is quite good, and Lundgren's
physical acting is perfect for the character

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.080
of He-Man, even if you can't always understand
what he's saying.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:08.820
"Gwildor, can this device of yours get us
to Greyskull?"

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:09.420
"Certainly!"

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.060
"To the sorceress?!"

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:16.040
Honestly, that kind of sums up the whole movie:
it doesn't always makes sense, but you want

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:16.800
to keep looking at it.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:18.340
Howard the Duck

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:22.460
Howard the Duck is remembered as one of the
biggest bombs of all time.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:26.500
Based on the Marvel comic by Steve Gerber,
it was intended to be an animated film.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:31.410
However, producer George Lucas owed Universal
a big summer release, so he decided to just

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:35.740
have his special effects people build a duck
suit and make the film live action.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:40.660
The movie starts as an off-kilter comedy and
then escalates into an action film until it

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:43.440
climaxes with a battle against a giant monster.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:48.060
Unfortunately it lacks the strong writing
and cast of veteran comedians needed to make

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:48.860
that all work.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:52.460
Nevertheless, Howard the Duck is a worth a
watch just for how weird it is.

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:55.240
"Don't shed any tears, toots!"

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:57.190
"You can wallow in your own self-pity!"

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:57.979
"Yeah, right!"

